<title>FRANCE: Ciments Francais 9-month sales slip.</title>
<headline>Ciments Francais 9-month sales slip.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					9,183     vs    9,584</p>
<p>	 - France				   4,460     vs    4,861</p>
<p>	 - EU excluding France		  1,535     vs    1,696</p>
<p>	 - Other countries			3,188     vs    3,027</p>
<p>Breakdown by sector</p>
<p>	 - Cement				   5,806     vs    5,772</p>
<p>	 - Construction materials	     3,377     vs    3,812</p>
<p>Note - Ciments Francais gave the results in a statement. It said sales fell 4.2 percent compared with the corresponding year earlier period. Sales were also down 4.2 percent on a comparable size and exchange rate basis.</p>
<p>The company said business levels remained depressed throughout the European Union (EU), particularly in France and Belgium. But business continued to be firm outside the EU, notably in North America and Morocco. Sales of the cement sector remained stable for the first nine months of 1996 while those of the constructions material sector declined in almost all markets. This decrease was particularly sharp in France and Belgium.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
